# Resuming project work

Consolidated September 17, 2026. Start from the current task and the relevant
owner below; this page does not impose a separate constraint set.

- [Current state and work](../memories/todos.md): baseline, review outcomes,
  remaining substantive work and whether the proposed sprint has started.
- [Attributed project decisions](project-facts.md): thesis scope, advisor flow,
  reproduction expectations and archive choices, with dates and limitations.
- [Thesis entry](../thesis/README.md): active source and build.
- [Authoring evidence](../memories/authoring-workflow.md) and
  [planning context](../memories/planning-context.md): observed writing failures,
  review expectations and unvalidated workflow proposals.
- [Proposed sprint](sprint-two/KICKOFF.md): its budget and coordination proposal;
  [readiness](sprint-two/readiness.md) owns dated resource observations.

The former report here copied these owners and the instructions of one reporting
turn. Its report-only scope, delegation restriction, tool availability and clock
were session observations, not durable project policy. The September 17
consolidation request explicitly asks for parallel work. Future sessions should
use their actual instructions and available tools rather than inherit those
old execution constraints.

The report also recorded an unresolved timing incident: its original recap had
a 120-second limit, but no start time was recorded. The first explicit reading,
September 17 at 06:32:32 UTC, was too late to establish compliance. This is a
historical limitation of that report, not a current deadline.
